id=dirtysepbypass
name=DirtySepolicy Bypass
version=v4.2.1
versionCode=42010
author=local
description=Defeats DirtySepolicy up to v2.2 and the Duck-Detector probe set. Intercepts selinuxfs access/status/context/policy and libselinux APIs, serves scrubbed /proc/{self,thread-self,<pid>}/maps/smaps/smaps_rollup/status/comm/stat/sched/mountinfo/mounts/environ, linker solists, fd links and env vars so ordinary apps cannot find the Zygisk injection, blocks same-uid cross-process /proc reads (forked cat, process_vm_readv, ptrace) by re-clearing PR_SET_DUMPABLE after specialization while keeping stock stat/prctl answers, and drops leaking AVC audit records from __android_log_* and logcat streams (ZN-AuditPatch style, without ZygiskNext).
updateJson=
